DELIMITER //

CREATE PROCEDURE procedure_name

   @param1 datatype,

   @param2 datatype

 BEGIN

   -- SQL_statements to be executed

   SELECT column1, column2

   FROM table_name

   WHERE columnN = @paramN;

END //

DELIMITER;

To run a stored procedure, use the CALL 
statement:

 CALL procedure_name('value1', 'value2');

To delete a stored procedure, use the DROP PROCEDURE statement:

 DROP PROCEDURE procedure_name;

Tip: To ensure that DROP PROCEDURE does not 
return an error, if the procedure is missing, add the IF EXISTS clause:

 DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS procedure_name;

